# Kids content separation

Kids section is a **navigation/content layer**, not purchase logic.

## Source of truth

`apps/storefront/src/lib/kids.ts`:
- `KIDS_ROOM_TYPE`
- `resolveKidsProducts()`

## Rules

- Kids-only = in ≥1 kids room set AND in NO non-kids room sets
- Cross-section products stay in main catalog / adult cart group
- `/kids/catalog` = kids-only only; `/catalog` excludes kids-only IDs
- Same criterion for include/exclude/cart grouping — no drift
- Shared cart/checkout; do **not** use ProductClassification for kids split
- Do **not** create separate kids cart/checkout
- Narrow `/kids/catalog` is known MVP; long-term needs explicit kids flag in data model

## Cart grouping

- `product_id` in kids set → “Woodright Kids”; else “Woodright”
- If kids resolution fails → ungrouped (no broken UI)
- Totals / remove / checkout CTA stay shared
